course: dictionary
lesson: 12855
title: Enforcement: making sure rules are kept
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enforcement is the word for making sure people obey a law or a rule. It also means punishing those who do not. Think of it as the job of checking that rules are kept. «The council increased the enforcement of the parking rules this month.» The sentence tells you the council is checking more carefully, so enforcement means checking that people follow the rules.
explain: You will often see enforcement with other words beside it. «Law enforcement» means the police and other officers whose job is to make people obey the law. «Strict enforcement» means the rules are checked very hard. Try the clue words first. If the sentence is about police, cameras or wardens checking things, enforcement is about making people obey.
explain: Enforcement is a noun, and it is uncountable. You cannot say «two enforcements». Instead, you talk about enforcement in general, or about a particular kind of enforcement, like «speed camera enforcement».
fact: Enforcement means making sure that people obey a law or a rule.
fact: Enforcement can also mean punishing people who break the rule.
fact: «Law enforcement» means the police and other officers who make people obey the law.
fact: «Strict enforcement» means checking very hard that a rule is kept.
fact: Enforcement is uncountable, so you do not add an s to it.
exercise: «Speed cameras help with the enforcement of the speed limit.» What does enforcement mean here? | Writing a letter to the council | *Making sure people obey the rule, and punishing those who do not | Painting new lines on the road | Making a rule for the first time
exercise: What is law enforcement? | The people who make new laws in Parliament | A school where children learn about the law | A book with all the rules in it | *The police and other officers whose job is to make people obey the law
exercise: «The town needs strict enforcement of the parking rules.» Which word tells you the checking is firm and not soft? | *strict | parking | the | rules
test: «The new rule needs strict enforcement.» What does strict enforcement mean? | Telling jokes about the rule | Changing the rule every day | *Checking hard that people follow the rule | Forgetting about the rule
test: Parking wardens check cars and give fines. Which kind of work is this? | Cooking food | *Law enforcement | Gardening | Writing poems
exam: Why does a town need enforcement officers? | *To make people obey the rules, and to punish those who do not | To build new houses for families | To teach children how to draw | To stop the rain from falling
